Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:27:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(auth): accept a reopened walled window whose reset moved
 later [daveey]

A redeemed banked/upstream reset reopens the weekly window with a later reset than
the persisted wall (#43747), so exact reset matching would keep a usable account
benched for days. Evidence now needs an open window resetting no earlier than the
persisted wall (60 s tolerance); a short window resetting before it still proves
nothing, so the 03:07Z short-window false positive stays benched.

Proof: boundary params (-61 s false, +7 d true, -6 d false); #43747 pool-selection
test now uses a moved reset. 6 focused files / 88 tests pass; 279 consumer files /
4933 passed, 2 failed in tests/e2e/core/providers/test_oauth_device_flow.py poll
cadence (timing under -j16 load; untouched code; passes isolated).
